# Validate against held-out writing

## Scope and existing evidence

Historical implementation notes describe domain-only evidence. The finite
acceptance below does not claim full sampling, rendering or quality testing.

Measure geometry, rhythm, joins, spacing, punctuation, and perceptual fidelity
against samples excluded from extraction and publish known failure modes.

Current executable evidence now freezes a transport-neutral held-out quality
report with those six required dimensions, caller-owned measured values and
supporting evidence, and caller-owned known failure modes. Structural admission
first rejects conflicting calibration sample roles, then rejects measurements
that reference training or unknown samples in report order, and finally requires
all six quality dimensions. Repeated held-out measurements and an empty known-
failure list remain valid because aggregation and failure discovery are not
inferred here. Successful structural admission now also produces
constructor-sealed evidence borrowing the exact sample declarations and report.

A 793-case compact oracle exhausts all 64 required-dimension subsets plus all
729 six-measurement held-out/training/unknown sample-reference sequences. Both
the direct and sealed paths pin role-conflict, first invalid-reference, then
missing-dimension precedence without declaring any quality score.

Metric units, thresholds, scoring, statistical/perceptual models, sample
sufficiency, quality-report generation, and pass/fail policy remain open.

## Finite held-out single-page quality comparison contract

**Inputs:** a corrected one-page held-out handwriting capture, stable held-out
sample IDs not used in training, one rendered proposed page from the same
accepted semantic source, the selected profile/revision and a declared
measurement method for each required quality dimension. **Outputs:** a
six-dimension report plus a finite readability/collision/style rubric, exact
known failures, and `Supported`, `NeedsReview` or `TheoryOnly` disposition.
Structural report completeness alone is never proof of personal fidelity.

**Sample split and page:** reserve `train-1` through `train-10` exclusively
for calibration and `hold-1` for an A4 page written without access to those
stroke samples. The held-out page repeats a finite corpus: title `Biología`,
a sentence `¿Dónde estás?`, digits `0123`, equation `x² + 1`, and a two-line
free-writing region. Record writing instrument, paper, photo geometry,
physical units, author consent and known calibration/capture limitations.

**Six required measurements:** `Geometry` (median baseline/height deviation
in mm), `Rhythm` (advance/velocity pattern deviation with observed method),
`Joins` (matched or mismatched contact transitions), `Spacing` (word/line
separation in mm), `Punctuation` (missing/reversed symbol count), and
`PerceptualFidelity` (explicitly labeled blinded human comparison or unknown).
All six carry exact `hold-1` provenance; training-only samples cannot fill a
missing axis. If rendered samples or human judgments are unavailable, mark
measurements as `Unmeasured` and return `TheoryOnly`, not invented scores.

**Finite first-release rubric (proposed):**

| Dimension | Observed pass condition | Refusal/review condition |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Legibility | Every corpus token readable | Any ambiguous token = review |
| Collision | No glyph/line overlap | Any observed overlap = block |
| Style | Blinded comparison recorded | No real evidence = theory-only |

**Worked example:** `hold-1` was never used for stroke extraction. Geometry
reports median 0.4 mm baseline deviation, punctuation reports 0 missing
symbols and Joins reports 1 mismatch in 8 observed transitions; record
all these illustrative numbers with exact method and source ID. One failed
join yields `NeedsReview` even if punctuation is complete and legibility is
rated acceptable. Missing real held-out capture yields `TheoryOnly` with no
claims of measured geometry, similarity or writer fidelity.

**Refusal example:** a report citing `train-3`, duplicate sample identity
across training and held-out, omitted `Rhythm` dimension, unresolved capture
scale, or an unmarked perceptual guess cannot become `Supported`. Preserve
all six dimensions and known failure modes in caller order; publish the
failure instead of silently changing the corpus or training on the holdout.
No matching score is promised without genuinely independent physical data.

**Assumptions and limits:** code already checks sample role separation,
held-out-only references and coverage of all six report dimensions, with
constructor-owned structural evidence. Actual comparison geometry, rendering,
human judgment, quality thresholds, sufficiency tests and scoring are absent.
This acceptance is deliberately theoretical where physical samples cannot be
collected or compared; it does not certify handwriting authenticity.

## Acceptance decision

- **Basis:** practical for source split/dimension completeness; theoretical
  for quality rubric and physical comparison, 2026-11-02.
- **Delivered:** one-page corpus, six measured axes, three-row rubric,
  example with a failing join and explicit `TheoryOnly` refusal.
- **Not implemented by this acceptance:** actual held-out measurement,
  perceptual scoring, calibration sufficiency or real-writer certification.
